    {
      "en": "This is Sad. Like 's' in 'sun', but push your tongue to the roof of your mouth — deeper, heavier!",
      "title": "Meet Sad!",
      "ar": "ص",
      "aud": "c-0-ar",
      "tr": "Sad"
    },
    {
      "en": "A large oval loop with a small tooth on top and a tail extending to the right. Sad looks like a big CIRCLE with a bump — it's the heavy version of Sin!",
      "title": "How to write Sad"
    },
    {
      "en": "With a fatha, Sad says “sa”.",
      "title": "Sad with fatha",
      "ar": "صَ",
      "aud": "c-2-ar"
    },
    {
      "en": "With a kasra, Sad says “se”.",
      "title": "Sad with kasra",
      "ar": "صِ",
      "aud": "c-3-ar"
    },
    {
      "en": "With a damma, Sad says “so”.",
